From 513a587ded9358e3708128c919e8632631734ed3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ice <icex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:18:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] account: who is signed in, and a --header escape hatch for
 the probe

A launcher has to be able to say whose library it is showing. The gamertag is
already a claim on any XSTS token, so it costs nothing; the gamerpic is not,
and lives on the profile service.

That service is the reason this is a command rather than something a caller
assembles out of `collections`: without `x-xbl-contract-version` it answers
401, not 400. A 401 reads as a token problem, so the missing header sends you
chasing auth instead of headers. Adding `--header NAME:VALUE` to the probe is
what made that visible, and it stays, because the next XBL service with its own
request shape should not need another command.

The profile call is best-effort. The token already yields a usable answer, so a
profile service that is down costs the picture, not the identity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
